<title>USA: Mississippi sees 9 pct rise in gaming tax revenue.</title>
<headline>Mississippi sees 9 pct rise in gaming tax revenue.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mississippi collected $157.7 million in gambling tax revenues in the fiscal year that ended June 30, a 9 percent increase over the prior year, the state Gaming Commission said.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect the growth to continue as we talk about air services, new hotel rooms and other amenities being added to the properties,&quot; Gaming Commission Spokesman Warren Strain told the Mississippi Sun Herald.</p>
<p>The state's 29 state-regulated casinos returned $75.8 million in tax revenues to local governments during the year.</p>
<p>(--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
